        "original_id": "cca9926d-2a9a-512d-abd4-20815347a8d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Phellodendron, Boltonia, Huáng bǎi\n- Taxonomy: Rutaceae, sunflower family, deciduous trees, genus, species\n- Places: East Asia, northeast Asia, North America, eastern Asia\n\nFacts:\n- Phellodendron, also called cork-tree, is a genus of deciduous trees in the family Rutaceae native to east and northeast Asia.\n- Boltonia is a genus of plants in the sunflower family native primarily to North America, with one species in eastern Asia.\n- Huáng bǎi, also known as Cortex Phellodendri, is the bark of either Phellodendron amurense or Phellodendron chinense.",
